response:
**Gates before launch**

First, I check that `pwd` and `git remote -v` point at this repo and that `git status --porcelain` is clean. I also confirm that `git log -1 -- spe/predictions/r04.yaml spe/plans/r04.md` shows the commit from 10 minutes ago and that neither file has changed since. Next, I save the script as `spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js` and commit it locally on its own. That commit is the eval step's commit, and it lands after the predictions commit. Then I test `grade.py`. Graded against `answers.json` itself, it must score 100%. Graded against a fixture with every label shifted by one, it must score 0%. A grader that cannot tell those two apart would make every number in this round meaningless. Then I launch with `args.smoke = true`. That runs 2 tickets x 1 trial x both configs and writes to `spe/evals/runs/r04-smoke/`. The smoke run proves the runner works and that the judge prompt never shows a config name. It also gives me the measured cost per run and per judge call for `args.estCostPerRun` and `args.estCostPerJudge`. Last, I check the projected spend. The full launch goes ahead only if 500 runs plus 500 judge calls plus overhead come in under $40. The script also refuses to start if that check fails. I did not open `r03-workflow.js`, so I assumed the per-run command is `node spe/evals/harness/run-config.js --config <id> --ticket <id> --trial <n> --out <path>`. If r03 used a different command, pass it in `args.runner`.

**spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js**

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'spe-r04-eval',
  description: 'SPE round 4. Configs B (12-line prompt, 6 tools) and C2 (12-line prompt, 3 tools + check_status). 50 tickets x 5 trials. Code grader for label.category and label.priority. Blind Opus judge for reply tone. Spend cap $40.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Preflight' },
    { title: 'Run' },
    { title: 'Grade' },
    { title: 'Judge' },
    { title: 'Report' },
  ],
};

// ---------- fixed by the approved r04 plan ----------
const CONFIGS = ['B', 'C2'];
const TICKETS_EXPECTED = 50;
const TRIALS_FULL = 5;
const SPEND_CAP_USD = 40;
const ANSWERS = 'spe/evals/tasks/answers.json';
const GRADER = 'spe/evals/graders/grade.py';
const JUDGE_RUBRIC = 'spe/evals/graders/judge.md';
const PREDICTIONS = 'spe/predictions/r04.yaml';
const PLAN = 'spe/plans/r04.md';

// ---------- launch arguments ----------
const A = args || {};
const SMOKE = Boolean(A.smoke);
const RUNNER = A.runner || 'node spe/evals/harness/run-config.js';
const RUN_DIR = SMOKE ? 'spe/evals/runs/r04-smoke' : 'spe/evals/runs/r04';
const TRIALS = SMOKE ? 1 : TRIALS_FULL;
const EST_RUN = SMOKE ? 0 : Number(A.estCostPerRun);
const EST_JUDGE = SMOKE ? 0 : Number(A.estCostPerJudge);
const OVERHEAD = SMOKE ? 0 : Number(A.estOverhead ?? 1.5); // preflight, grade, summary agents
const CHUNK = Math.max(2, 2 * Math.floor(Number(A.chunk ?? 20) / 2)); // even, so B and C2 stay paired
const MAX_INFRA_ERROR_RATE = 0.1;

if (!SMOKE && !(EST_RUN > 0 && EST_JUDGE > 0)) {
  throw new Error('Pass args.estCostPerRun and args.estCostPerJudge, measured from the smoke run.');
}

// ---------- helpers ----------
function rng(seed) {
  let s = seed >>> 0;
  return () => { s = (s * 1664525 + 1013904223) >>> 0; return s / 4294967296; };
}
function shuffle(xs, seed) {
  const r = rng(seed); const a = xs.slice();
  for (let i = a.length - 1; i > 0; i--) { const j = Math.floor(r() * (i + 1)); [a[i], a[j]] = [a[j], a[i]]; }
  return a;
}
function chunks(xs, n) { const out = []; for (let i = 0; i < xs.length; i += n) out.push(xs.slice(i, i + n)); return out; }
const key = (c) => `${c.config}|${c.ticket}|${c.trial}`;
const pct = (num, den) => (den ? Math.round((1000 * num) / den) / 10 : null);

// ---------- schemas ----------
const PREFLIGHT_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    ok: { type: 'boolean' },
    problems: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    ticketIds: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    predictionsCommit: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['ok', 'problems', 'ticketIds', 'predictionsCommit'],
};
const RUN_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    status: { type: 'string', enum: ['ok', 'infra_error'] },
    outPath: { type: 'string' },
    reply: { type: 'string' },
    error: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['status', 'outPath', 'reply', 'error'],
};
const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    graderCommand: { type: 'string' },
    rows: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          config: { type: 'string' },
          ticket: { type: 'string' },
          trial: { type: 'integer' },
          categoryOk: { type: 'boolean' },
          priorityOk: { type: 'boolean' },
        },
        required: ['config', 'ticket', 'trial', 'categoryOk', 'priorityOk'],
      },
    },
  },
  required: ['graderCommand', 'rows'],
};
const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    score: { type: 'number' },
    pass: { type: 'boolean' },
    reason: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['score', 'pass', 'reason'],
};
const WRITE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: { written: { type: 'boolean' }, path: { type: 'string' } },
  required: ['written', 'path'],
};

// ========== Preflight ==========
phase('Preflight');
const pre = await agent(
  `You are the preflight check for SPE round 4. Read only. Do not edit, stage, or commit anything.
1. Run "git status --porcelain". Report any changes under spe/ as a problem.
2. Confirm ${PREDICTIONS} and ${PLAN} are committed and have no changes since their commit. Run "git log -1 --format=%H -- ${PREDICTIONS}" and return that hash as predictionsCommit.
3. Confirm ${GRADER}, ${JUDGE_RUBRIC}, and ${ANSWERS} exist.
4. Confirm the runner "${RUNNER}" exists and accepts --config B and --config C2. Use its --help or a config listing. Do not run a real ticket.
5. Read ${ANSWERS} and return every ticket id in file order as ticketIds. Report a problem if the count is not ${TICKETS_EXPECTED}.
6. Report a problem if ${RUN_DIR} already holds run files. Old runs would mix into this round.
Set ok to true only if problems is empty.`,
  { label: 'preflight', phase: 'Preflight', schema: PREFLIGHT_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' },
);
if (!pre.ok) {
  log(`Preflight failed: ${pre.problems.join(' | ')}`);
  throw new Error('Preflight failed. Nothing was run.');
}
const tickets = SMOKE ? pre.ticketIds.slice(0, 2) : pre.ticketIds;
log(`Preflight ok. predictions commit ${pre.predictionsCommit}. ${tickets.length} tickets, ${TRIALS} trial(s), smoke=${SMOKE}.`);

// Order: trial, then ticket, then config. A stop at any point leaves B and C2 balanced.
const cells = [];
for (let t = 1; t <= TRIALS; t++) for (const id of tickets) for (const c of CONFIGS) cells.push({ config: c, ticket: id, trial: t });

const perCell = EST_RUN + EST_JUDGE; // reserve judge cost when a run launches
const projected = OVERHEAD + cells.length * perCell;
log(`Projected spend $${projected.toFixed(2)} against cap $${SPEND_CAP_USD}.`);
if (!SMOKE && projected > SPEND_CAP_USD && !A.allowPartial) {
  throw new Error(`Projected $${projected.toFixed(2)} exceeds the $${SPEND_CAP_USD} cap. Revisit the plan or pass args.allowPartial.`);
}

// ========== Run ==========
phase('Run');
const runPrompt = (c) => `You execute one eval run for SPE round 4. You are a harness operator, not the system under test.
Run exactly this command once:
  ${RUNNER} --config ${c.config} --ticket ${c.ticket} --trial ${c.trial} --out ${RUN_DIR}/${c.config}/${c.ticket}-t${c.trial}.json
Rules:
- Do not edit the config, its prompt, its tools, the ticket, or any file outside ${RUN_DIR}.
- Do not judge or fix the answer. Do not re-run because the label looks wrong.
- Retry once only for an infrastructure failure (timeout, rate limit, 5xx, crash before output). If the retry also fails, return status "infra_error" and put the message in error.
- On success return status "ok", the outPath, and the final customer reply text exactly as written in the output file. Set error to "".`;

let spent = OVERHEAD;
let stoppedEarly = false;
const runs = [];
for (const batch of chunks(cells, CHUNK)) {
  const cost = batch.length * perCell;
  if (spent + cost > SPEND_CAP_USD) {
    stoppedEarly = true;
    log(`Spend cap reached at about $${spent.toFixed(2)}. Stopping before run ${runs.length + 1} of ${cells.length}.`);
    break;
  }
  spent += cost;
  const results = await parallel(batch.map((c) => async () => {
    try {
      const r = await agent(runPrompt(c), {
        label: `run ${c.config} ${c.ticket} t${c.trial}`, phase: 'Run', schema: RUN_SCHEMA, model: 'opus',
      });
      return { ...c, ...r };
    } catch (e) {
      return { ...c, status: 'infra_error', outPath: '', reply: '', error: String(e) };
    }
  }));
  runs.push(...results);
  const bad = results.filter((r) => r.status !== 'ok').length;
  log(`Runs ${runs.length}/${cells.length}. Batch infra errors ${bad}/${results.length}. Est spend $${spent.toFixed(2)}.`);
  if (bad / results.length > MAX_INFRA_ERROR_RATE) {
    stoppedEarly = true;
    log('Infra error rate above 10% in one batch. Stopping so the budget is not spent on a broken harness.');
    break;
  }
}
const okRuns = runs.filter((r) => r.status === 'ok');

// ========== Grade ==========
phase('Grade');
const grade = await agent(
  `Run the round 4 code grader. Do not modify ${GRADER} or ${ANSWERS}.
Grade every run file under ${RUN_DIR}/B/ and ${RUN_DIR}/C2/ with ${GRADER} against ${ANSWERS}. The grader checks label.category and label.priority.
If you are unsure of the grader's arguments, read its --help or its argparse block first. Return the exact command you ran as graderCommand.
Return one row per run file. Each row holds config (the folder name), ticket, trial (from the file name <ticket>-t<trial>.json), categoryOk, and priorityOk, exactly as the grader reports them. Do not recompute or override the grader.`,
  { label: 'grade', phase: 'Grade', schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' },
);
const gradeByKey = new Map(grade.rows.map((r) => [key(r), r]));
const missingGrades = okRuns.filter((r) => !gradeByKey.has(key(r))).map(key);
if (missingGrades.length) log(`Warning: ${missingGrades.length} ok runs have no grade row. First few: ${missingGrades.slice(0, 5).join(', ')}`);

// ========== Judge (blind, shuffled) ==========
phase('Judge');
const judgeItems = shuffle(okRuns, 404).map((r, i) => ({ ...r, jid: `j${String(i + 1).padStart(3, '0')}` }));
const judgePrompt = (r) => `You are the tone judge for item ${r.jid}.
Read ${JUDGE_RUBRIC} and apply it exactly. Read ticket ${r.ticket} from the ticket source that ${ANSWERS} points to, for context only.
Do not open anything under spe/evals/runs/. Do not try to find out which configuration wrote this reply.
Reply to judge:
<<<REPLY
${r.reply}
REPLY>>>
Return score on the scale judge.md defines, pass as judge.md defines it, and a reason of one or two sentences.`;

const judged = [];
for (const batch of chunks(judgeItems, CHUNK)) {
  const results = await parallel(batch.map((r) => async () => {
    try {
      const j = await agent(judgePrompt(r), { label: `judge ${r.jid}`, phase: 'Judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' });
      return { ...r, judge: j };
    } catch (e) {
      return { ...r, judge: null, judgeError: String(e) };
    }
  }));
  judged.push(...results);
}
const judgeByKey = new Map(judged.map((r) => [key(r), r]));

// ========== Report ==========
phase('Report');
function summarize(config) {
  const mine = runs.filter((r) => r.config === config);
  const ok = mine.filter((r) => r.status === 'ok');
  const g = ok.map((r) => gradeByKey.get(key(r))).filter(Boolean);
  const j = ok.map((r) => judgeByKey.get(key(r))).filter((r) => r && r.judge).map((r) => r.judge);
  const both = (x) => x.categoryOk && x.priorityOk;

  const perTrial = [];
  for (let t = 1; t <= TRIALS; t++) {
    const gt = g.filter((x) => x.trial === t);
    perTrial.push(pct(gt.filter(both).length, gt.length));
  }
  // pass^k: share of tickets correct on every trial that was graded for them
  const byTicket = new Map();
  for (const x of g) { if (!byTicket.has(x.ticket)) byTicket.set(x.ticket, []); byTicket.get(x.ticket).push(both(x)); }
  const fullTickets = [...byTicket.values()].filter((v) => v.length === TRIALS);

  return {
    config,
    attempted: mine.length,
    ok: ok.length,
    infraErrors: mine.length - ok.length,
    graded: g.length,
    categoryAccPct: pct(g.filter((x) => x.categoryOk).length, g.length),
    priorityAccPct: pct(g.filter((x) => x.priorityOk).length, g.length),
    bothAccPct: pct(g.filter(both).length, g.length),
    bothAccPctByTrial: perTrial,
    passAllTrialsPct: pct(fullTickets.filter((v) => v.every(Boolean)).length, fullTickets.length),
    judged: j.length,
    toneMeanScore: j.length ? Math.round((100 * j.reduce((s, x) => s + x.score, 0)) / j.length) / 100 : null,
    tonePassPct: pct(j.filter((x) => x.pass).length, j.length),
  };
}

const summary = {
  round: 'r04',
  smoke: SMOKE,
  predictionsCommit: pre.predictionsCommit,
  graderCommand: grade.graderCommand,
  tickets: tickets.length,
  trialsPlanned: TRIALS,
  cellsPlanned: cells.length,
  cellsRun: runs.length,
  stoppedEarly,
  estSpendUsd: Math.round(spent * 100) / 100,
  spendCapUsd: SPEND_CAP_USD,
  missingGrades: missingGrades.length,
  judgeErrors: judged.filter((r) => !r.judge).length,
  configs: CONFIGS.map(summarize),
};

await agent(
  `Write this JSON, pretty-printed with 2-space indent, to ${RUN_DIR}/summary.json. Write nothing else. Do not stage or commit.
${JSON.stringify(summary)}`,
  { label: 'write summary', phase: 'Report', schema: WRITE_SCHEMA, model: 'opus' },
);

log(`r04 done. ${JSON.stringify(summary.configs)}`);
return summary;
```

When the run finishes, I commit `spe/evals/runs/r04/` locally as its own SPE step. The comparison against `spe/predictions/r04.yaml` starts after that commit.
